1
00:00:00,959 --> 00:00:03,795
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

2
00:00:03,878 --> 00:00:08,216
[MAMANG SASTRE PLAYING]

3
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:10,719
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

4
00:00:10,802 --> 00:00:12,846
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

5
00:00:16,725 --> 00:00:17,934
Atoy: I know, they're here too.

6
00:00:18,560 --> 00:00:19,310
Ah, I'll come to you.

7
00:00:19,394 --> 00:00:21,104
Emerson: I'll just leave this
cake, wait a moment.

8
00:00:21,187 --> 00:00:21,855
Atoy: Don't! What are
you doing?

9
00:00:21,938 --> 00:00:24,441
Your mission is to protect
Audrey's cake.

10
00:00:24,983 --> 00:00:26,609
Maybe we can just
go home.

11
00:00:26,693 --> 00:00:28,319
It's just the two of us here,
we have no backup.

12
00:00:28,903 --> 00:00:30,071
Atoy: I need to go see
Belladonna!

13
00:00:30,155 --> 00:00:31,698
You're still there?!

14
00:00:31,781 --> 00:00:34,617
Oh my, Atoy, what about
our family day?

15
00:00:34,701 --> 00:00:35,535
I'll follow, okay?

16
00:00:35,618 --> 00:00:37,203
On screen: No being late to
the games, okay.

17
00:00:37,287 --> 00:00:38,079
Goon 1: He's right
here, Boss.

18
00:00:38,163 --> 00:00:40,582
Artem: There's no way he can escape
from us anymore.

19
00:00:40,665 --> 00:00:41,791
Woman: Is he the husband?

20
00:00:41,875 --> 00:00:43,877
Because he's taking care
of the kids.

21
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,920
He's the best Uncle Oka.

22
00:00:46,004 --> 00:00:47,714
I just don't want to carry
the cake, Atoy.

23
00:00:47,797 --> 00:00:49,299
It's hard to run while carrying
something like that.

24
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:50,800
Let's just leave that!

25
00:00:50,884 --> 00:00:52,010
We can't leave this.

26
00:00:52,093 --> 00:00:53,762
Audrey will be
mad at me!

27
00:00:53,845 --> 00:00:54,512
Your older brothers?

28
00:00:54,596 --> 00:00:55,513
Give me Wanbol's money!

29
00:00:56,139 --> 00:00:56,765
Oscar: Hey.

30
00:00:56,848 --> 00:00:58,933
Don't ever let me see your faces
here again.

31
00:00:59,017 --> 00:01:00,226
Both: Yes, Sir.

32
00:01:00,310 --> 00:01:02,812
Ibyang: Even though Tatoy
isn't here,

33
00:01:02,896 --> 00:01:05,065
I feel like he's here.

34
00:01:05,690 --> 00:01:06,775
Ibyang: Because…

35
00:01:06,858 --> 00:01:10,361
you take care of and protect
me and Janine.

36
00:01:11,071 --> 00:01:11,654
[Oscar chuckles]

37
00:01:11,738 --> 00:01:13,782
The sack race!

38
00:01:13,865 --> 00:01:16,242
We can't join anymore.

39
00:01:16,326 --> 00:01:17,702
You can still join!

40
00:01:17,786 --> 00:01:19,037
So, while your Tatoy
isn't here,

41
00:01:19,120 --> 00:01:20,205
is it okay if I'm the
stand-in for now?

42
00:01:20,288 --> 00:01:21,664
Ame: Go, Team Padua!

43
00:01:25,043 --> 00:01:29,631
[music swells]

44
00:01:33,468 --> 00:01:37,889
[ominous music playing]

45
00:01:37,972 --> 00:01:38,890
Where is he?

46
00:01:39,432 --> 00:01:41,142
We just heard him
here earlier.

47
00:01:41,226 --> 00:01:42,393
[music continues]

48
00:01:43,895 --> 00:01:44,562
Find him.

49
00:01:45,563 --> 00:01:48,108
[tense music playing]

50
00:01:57,784 --> 00:02:00,495
[music swells]

51
00:02:03,998 --> 00:02:06,167
[music fades]

52
00:02:06,251 --> 00:02:07,335
[footsteps padding]

53
00:02:08,044 --> 00:02:12,298
[gunshots]

54
00:02:23,351 --> 00:02:24,769
Son of a thread.

55
00:02:26,062 --> 00:02:28,064
Even the cake got dragged
into this.

56
00:02:28,148 --> 00:02:29,732
This is the only souvenir
I got for them.

57
00:02:31,734 --> 00:02:32,402
Geez.

58
00:02:38,116 --> 00:02:39,534
[thuds]

59
00:02:40,118 --> 00:02:40,910
[groans]

60
00:02:40,994 --> 00:02:42,036
[grunts & groans]

61
00:02:42,120 --> 00:02:43,121
[gunshots]

62
00:02:43,663 --> 00:02:45,081
[tense music playing]

63
00:02:45,165 --> 00:02:46,124
[music fades]

64
00:03:08,187 --> 00:03:11,065
[grunting & groaning]

65
00:03:11,149 --> 00:03:14,152
[thumping & thudding]

66
00:03:15,194 --> 00:03:16,029
[gunshots]

67
00:03:16,112 --> 00:03:16,738
[groans]

68
00:03:16,821 --> 00:03:19,908
[grunts & groans]

69
00:03:22,410 --> 00:03:26,748
[sneaky music playing]

70
00:03:29,918 --> 00:03:31,002
Hey!

71
00:03:31,085 --> 00:03:32,587
[gunshots]

72
00:03:32,670 --> 00:03:33,963
[guns jams]

73
00:03:39,427 --> 00:03:41,012
It's our turn now!

74
00:03:42,764 --> 00:03:44,057
Bang! Bang! Bang!

75
00:03:44,849 --> 00:03:46,142
Oh, you're dead.

76
00:03:46,726 --> 00:03:52,315
[gunshots]

77
00:03:52,398 --> 00:03:57,070
[gunshots]

78
00:03:58,321 --> 00:03:59,239
[gun jams]

79
00:04:00,198 --> 00:04:03,117
[gunshots]

80
00:04:03,201 --> 00:04:04,369
[theme music playing]

81
00:04:04,452 --> 00:04:05,745
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor… ♪

82
00:04:05,828 --> 00:04:09,457
["Mamang Sastre" playing]

83
00:04:12,794 --> 00:04:14,254
♪ Wait a moment, Mr. Tailor ♪

84
00:04:14,337 --> 00:04:16,339
♪ Can you be the one to stitch up ♪

85
00:04:16,422 --> 00:04:17,715
♪ The hole in my polo

86
00:04:17,799 --> 00:04:20,551
that's right under the armpit ♪

87
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:22,553
♪ In every cut of cloth ♪

88
00:04:22,637 --> 00:04:24,305
♪ There’s a secret behind it ♪

89
00:04:24,389 --> 00:04:26,224
♪ If your measurement is wrong,

90
00:04:26,307 --> 00:04:31,479
the whole fit turns crooked… ♪

91
00:04:31,562 --> 00:04:33,231
♪ Oh, Mr. Tailor ♪

92
00:04:33,314 --> 00:04:35,525
♪ Holding the scissors ♪

93
00:04:36,150 --> 00:04:37,193
[music swells]

94
00:04:39,696 --> 00:04:40,822
[music fades]

95
00:04:41,364 --> 00:04:42,198
[cheering]

96
00:04:42,282 --> 00:04:47,287
Welcome to the champion edition
of the sack race!

97
00:04:47,370 --> 00:04:49,914
[cheering]

98
00:04:49,998 --> 00:04:53,084
It tends to be between
Team Padua

99
00:04:53,167 --> 00:04:56,462
and Team Gregorio!

100
00:04:56,546 --> 00:04:58,256
[lively chatter, cheering]

101
00:04:58,339 --> 00:04:59,632
Oh, here.

102
00:04:59,716 --> 00:05:00,883
Strategy, strategy.

103
00:05:01,426 --> 00:05:02,969
Janine, Ibyang, you two
in front.

104
00:05:03,052 --> 00:05:04,387
Mommy, we'll be at
the back.

105
00:05:04,470 --> 00:05:05,179
When I say jump,

106
00:05:05,263 --> 00:05:06,347
jump, jump, jump!

107
00:05:06,431 --> 00:05:08,141
Listen, we can do this.

108
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:10,184
Oscar: And then we turn
like that, okay.

109
00:05:10,268 --> 00:05:11,894
On your mark!

110
00:05:12,895 --> 00:05:16,149
Host: Ready, set, go!

111
00:05:16,232 --> 00:05:17,608
Jump, jump, jump,
jump,

112
00:05:17,692 --> 00:05:19,152
jump, jump,
jump, jump,

113
00:05:19,235 --> 00:05:20,570
jump, jump, jump,
jump,

114
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:22,447
jump, jump, jump,
jump, jump!

115
00:05:22,530 --> 00:05:24,032
[lively chatter, cheering]

116
00:05:24,115 --> 00:05:25,366
Jump, jump,
jump, jump,

117
00:05:25,450 --> 00:05:26,200
jump, jump--

118
00:05:27,577 --> 00:05:29,412
Jump, jump, jump, jump,
jump, jump!

119
00:05:30,538 --> 00:05:31,873
Yeah!

120
00:05:33,207 --> 00:05:34,459
Crowd: Team Padua!

121
00:05:34,542 --> 00:05:36,836
- My pleasure! Oh, Padua!
- Crowd: Team Padua!

122
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:39,213
Crowd: Team Padua!
Team Padua!

123
00:05:42,258 --> 00:05:43,259
Thanks for the help.

124
00:05:43,342 --> 00:05:44,135
Hey, my pleasure.

125
00:05:44,218 --> 00:05:46,179
I'll tell Atoy that we won.

126
00:05:46,262 --> 00:05:47,764
[muffled chattering]

127
00:05:49,182 --> 00:05:49,682
[whoops]

128
00:05:49,766 --> 00:05:52,226
Yeah! High five!

129
00:05:52,310 --> 00:05:54,103
[music continues]
[lively chatter]

130
00:05:54,187 --> 00:05:56,105
- Ah, Ame!
- Oscar: Ibyang, Ibyang, Ibyang!

131
00:05:56,189 --> 00:05:58,524
Where are Denden and Karla?

132
00:05:58,608 --> 00:06:00,193
Oh, Denden has a stomachache.

133
00:06:00,276 --> 00:06:01,360
Karla went with her.

134
00:06:01,944 --> 00:06:02,695
Poor thing.

135
00:06:03,237 --> 00:06:03,821
Oscar: Wow!

136
00:06:04,781 --> 00:06:06,157
Ame: Great job!

137
00:06:06,240 --> 00:06:06,741
[lively chatter, cheering]

138
00:06:06,824 --> 00:06:09,243
Still no word from Atoy.

139
00:06:09,327 --> 00:06:11,245
[applauds]

140
00:06:11,329 --> 00:06:12,497
Ame: Great job!

141
00:06:13,081 --> 00:06:14,332
Great job, ah, great!

142
00:06:14,415 --> 00:06:14,916
Yay!

143
00:06:14,999 --> 00:06:15,583
[whooping]

144
00:06:15,666 --> 00:06:17,919
- Oscar: Oh, I told you so!
- They’re tired, so tired!

145
00:06:18,002 --> 00:06:18,961
Audrey: Awesome, awesome.

146
00:06:19,045 --> 00:06:19,921
Ame: They’re tired.

147
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:22,215
[lively chatter, cheering]

148
00:06:22,298 --> 00:06:24,050
Yay! We won!

149
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:25,468
[music fades]

150
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:27,595
Lord, I'm ready, Lord.

151
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:30,223
Tonet, cool down my room up
there in heaven.

152
00:06:30,306 --> 00:06:32,016
[sneaky music playing]

153
00:06:32,100 --> 00:06:32,934
I'll see you soon.

154
00:06:33,017 --> 00:06:34,227
[gunshots]

155
00:06:34,310 --> 00:06:35,561
[groans]

156
00:06:35,645 --> 00:06:39,273
[gasping]

157
00:06:39,357 --> 00:06:42,151
[music swells]

158
00:06:42,985 --> 00:06:45,154
[music fades]

159
00:06:46,697 --> 00:06:49,742
[mysterious music playing]

160
00:06:51,619 --> 00:06:52,870
[clears throat]

161
00:06:52,954 --> 00:06:53,538
Ah, oh--

162
00:06:53,621 --> 00:06:56,332
Thank you for saving my life.

163
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,668
Are you Master Cutter?

164
00:07:00,169 --> 00:07:03,881
Ah, yeah. No. I am, ah…

165
00:07:03,965 --> 00:07:05,967
Oh, so you-- you speak Tagalog.

166
00:07:06,050 --> 00:07:06,968
I'm not Master Cutter.

167
00:07:07,051 --> 00:07:09,804
But I'm a Son of the
Thread, Emerson.

168
00:07:10,805 --> 00:07:11,722
So, where is Master Cutter?

169
00:07:12,223 --> 00:07:14,058
Th-- th-- there.

170
00:07:14,142 --> 00:07:15,226
We'll go back for him.

171
00:07:15,309 --> 00:07:15,977
Let's go back for him.

172
00:07:16,060 --> 00:07:16,978
Oh, let's go.

173
00:07:17,061 --> 00:07:18,187
Come, let's go back
for him.

174
00:07:18,271 --> 00:07:19,605
The-- the-- wait.

175
00:07:19,689 --> 00:07:20,773
[music fades]

176
00:07:21,482 --> 00:07:23,359
[pleasant music playing]
[chuckles]

177
00:07:25,945 --> 00:07:26,571
Let's go.

178
00:07:27,321 --> 00:07:28,072
[chuckles]

179
00:07:28,156 --> 00:07:30,116
That's what you get.
Right?

180
00:07:30,199 --> 00:07:31,868
You don't know how
to forgive.

181
00:07:31,951 --> 00:07:33,619
Mmm, this. There, there.

182
00:07:34,370 --> 00:07:35,246
Come on.

183
00:07:37,540 --> 00:07:38,666
[music fades]

184
00:07:40,126 --> 00:07:42,336
[ominous music playing]

185
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:55,391
[grunting & groaning]

186
00:07:55,475 --> 00:07:58,728
[thumping & thudding]

187
00:08:01,898 --> 00:08:03,065
Stay right there.

188
00:08:03,149 --> 00:08:04,275
We meet again, Atoy.

189
00:08:04,358 --> 00:08:05,860
This is your last day.

190
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:08,362
[grunting & groaning]

191
00:08:08,446 --> 00:08:11,699
[thumping & thudding]

192
00:08:11,782 --> 00:08:15,119
[groans, grunts]

193
00:08:15,703 --> 00:08:16,662
[grunts]

194
00:08:19,499 --> 00:08:23,544
[grunts & groans]

195
00:08:23,628 --> 00:08:27,673
[thumps & thuds]

196
00:08:31,427 --> 00:08:32,053
Atoy!

197
00:08:33,638 --> 00:08:34,180
[grunts]

198
00:08:34,263 --> 00:08:36,265
[thuds]

199
00:08:39,685 --> 00:08:43,814
[grunting]

200
00:08:44,357 --> 00:08:45,566
[grunts & groans]

201
00:08:46,150 --> 00:08:47,360
[thumps]

202
00:08:49,904 --> 00:08:51,781
You've been making things hard for
us for so long.

203
00:08:52,365 --> 00:08:53,407
I'll finish you now!

204
00:08:53,491 --> 00:08:54,367
Ah, is that so?

205
00:08:55,284 --> 00:08:56,202
I'm the one who's going
to finish you.

206
00:08:56,285 --> 00:08:57,745
[grunts & groans]

207
00:08:57,828 --> 00:08:59,330
[thumps, swishes & thuds]

208
00:09:02,124 --> 00:09:03,960
[gunshots]

209
00:09:07,797 --> 00:09:11,050
[suspicious music playing]

210
00:09:39,704 --> 00:09:40,871
Are you Belladonna?

211
00:09:41,706 --> 00:09:45,710
The temperature here is always
30 to 31 degrees Celsius.

212
00:09:45,793 --> 00:09:46,460
It’s hot.

213
00:09:46,544 --> 00:09:48,212
[music continues]

214
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,714
Yes, yes, yes. It's-- it's--

215
00:09:49,797 --> 00:09:50,965
Hot, it's really hot.

216
00:09:51,048 --> 00:09:53,134
Especially when you’re chasing after
your enemies.

217
00:09:53,217 --> 00:09:55,011
Tracker 124, The Master Cutter.

218
00:09:55,094 --> 00:09:57,555
Ex Obs, Beatriz Davos.

219
00:09:57,638 --> 00:09:59,056
Code name, Belladonna.

220
00:10:00,641 --> 00:10:01,475
[music fades]

221
00:10:02,059 --> 00:10:03,060
[clears throat]

222
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,312
Ah, Son of the Thread.

223
00:10:04,395 --> 00:10:06,647
Code name, Thread 1.

224
00:10:06,731 --> 00:10:09,483
Real name, Emerson Mendoza.

225
00:10:09,567 --> 00:10:10,943
[sneaky music playing]

226
00:10:11,819 --> 00:10:13,446
[phone ringing]

227
00:10:15,031 --> 00:10:16,991
[ominous music playing]

228
00:10:33,799 --> 00:10:35,468
Samir on the phone: Artem…

229
00:10:35,551 --> 00:10:38,262
Give me an update on Atoy
and Belladonna.

230
00:10:39,180 --> 00:10:40,181
Artem is dead.

231
00:10:40,264 --> 00:10:41,682
[music continues]

232
00:10:41,766 --> 00:10:44,602
I'm always five steps ahead
of you, Samir.

233
00:10:44,685 --> 00:10:45,936
[music continues]

234
00:10:46,437 --> 00:10:48,898
Is that what you
think?

235
00:10:49,815 --> 00:10:50,650
Hmm?

236
00:10:53,986 --> 00:10:55,780
[music swells]

237
00:10:56,947 --> 00:10:58,074
[music fades]

238
00:10:58,699 --> 00:11:00,201
[soft rock music playing]

239
00:11:01,786 --> 00:11:03,788
Wow, ah, five steps.

240
00:11:04,789 --> 00:11:05,665
Wow.

241
00:11:05,748 --> 00:11:07,041
Let's go. We got to go.

242
00:11:07,750 --> 00:11:09,627
Is Mama Emma safe?

243
00:11:09,710 --> 00:11:10,419
Yes, she's safe.

244
00:11:11,420 --> 00:11:12,713
Audrey's cake is safe too.

245
00:11:12,797 --> 00:11:13,923
Ah, let's go.

246
00:11:14,006 --> 00:11:15,674
Thank you. Let's go.

247
00:11:16,342 --> 00:11:18,552
Cita: Go, Janine!
Go, Ibyang!

248
00:11:18,636 --> 00:11:20,137
[lively chatter, cheering]

249
00:11:20,638 --> 00:11:23,099
Ame: Go! Go, go, go!

250
00:11:23,182 --> 00:11:25,101
Cita: Go, Janine!
Go, Ibyang!

251
00:11:26,018 --> 00:11:27,728
Go, Ibyang, Janine!

252
00:11:28,854 --> 00:11:30,731
[lively chatter, giggling]

253
00:11:30,815 --> 00:11:31,941
[upbeat music playing]

254
00:11:32,024 --> 00:11:33,359
[exclaiming]

255
00:11:35,736 --> 00:11:39,657
[exclaiming]

256
00:11:39,740 --> 00:11:41,617
[light music playing]

257
00:11:41,700 --> 00:11:42,368
Oh no!

258
00:11:42,993 --> 00:11:48,332
[lively chatter, exclaiming]

259
00:11:48,416 --> 00:11:50,418
Flores family, thank you!

260
00:11:51,961 --> 00:11:54,380
- For you.
- Padua kids, sorry!

261
00:11:54,463 --> 00:11:56,215
[lively chatter]

262
00:11:56,298 --> 00:11:58,092
Okay, fight.

263
00:11:58,175 --> 00:11:59,593
So, the remaining pairs are…

264
00:11:59,677 --> 00:12:03,097
Team Montinola and
Team Padua!

265
00:12:03,180 --> 00:12:05,516
[cheering]

266
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:07,893
Please fold your
papers again

267
00:12:07,977 --> 00:12:09,520
for our final round.

268
00:12:09,603 --> 00:12:10,896
[lively chatter]

269
00:12:10,980 --> 00:12:11,730
Audrey: Okay.

270
00:12:11,814 --> 00:12:13,149
[overlapping chatter]

271
00:12:13,232 --> 00:12:14,275
Oh no! That's so hard!

272
00:12:14,358 --> 00:12:15,025
[titters]

273
00:12:15,109 --> 00:12:16,402
[lively chatter, cheering]
[upbeat music playing]

274
00:12:16,485 --> 00:12:17,611
Go, Audrey!

275
00:12:17,695 --> 00:12:18,696
[exclaims]

276
00:12:18,779 --> 00:12:19,697
Oka!

277
00:12:19,780 --> 00:12:20,739
Why don't we just do it!

278
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:22,450
Go, Uncle Oka!

279
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:23,617
[exclaims]

280
00:12:23,701 --> 00:12:25,077
Crowd: Team Padua!

281
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:26,412
Team Padua! Team Padua!

282
00:12:26,495 --> 00:12:27,913
Just one more!

283
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:32,918
Crowd: Team Padua!
Team Padua!

284
00:12:33,586 --> 00:12:35,337
- Team Padua! Team Padua!
- Audrey: What do we do now?

285
00:12:36,630 --> 00:12:38,132
Crowd: Team Padua!
Team Padua!

286
00:12:38,215 --> 00:12:41,010
[exclaiming]
Go, go, go, go! Go, Uncle!

287
00:12:41,093 --> 00:12:45,097
Host: And the winner again
is Team Padua!

288
00:12:45,181 --> 00:12:47,516
[exclaiming & cheering]

289
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:49,935
[light music playing]

290
00:12:50,019 --> 00:12:51,520
Yay!

291
00:12:54,398 --> 00:12:58,319
Crowd: Team Padua!
Team Padua!

292
00:12:58,402 --> 00:13:01,655
- Yeah!
- Crowd: Team Padua!

293
00:13:01,739 --> 00:13:02,865
Yay! Yay!

294
00:13:02,948 --> 00:13:03,532
What?

295
00:13:03,616 --> 00:13:05,159
Thank you, Oka.

296
00:13:05,951 --> 00:13:07,745
Even without Atoy,

297
00:13:07,828 --> 00:13:09,413
we made the kids happy.

298
00:13:10,039 --> 00:13:11,624
I told you I'd take
care of you.

299
00:13:11,707 --> 00:13:12,833
[chuckles]

300
00:13:12,917 --> 00:13:13,542
Hey!

301
00:13:13,626 --> 00:13:14,668
Family picture, come on!

302
00:13:14,752 --> 00:13:15,419
Who has a phone?

303
00:13:15,503 --> 00:13:16,504
Just a group picture,

304
00:13:16,587 --> 00:13:17,505
not a family picture.

305
00:13:18,964 --> 00:13:20,257
Just a group picture.

306
00:13:20,758 --> 00:13:22,051
I don't have a phone…

307
00:13:22,134 --> 00:13:22,760
Do you have a phone?

308
00:13:22,843 --> 00:13:23,344
Ah, okay. We'll just
use mine.

309
00:13:23,427 --> 00:13:24,303
Ah, here.

310
00:13:24,386 --> 00:13:25,387
Here, me. I have
a monopod.

311
00:13:25,471 --> 00:13:25,971
Me, I'll take it.

312
00:13:26,055 --> 00:13:26,805
Audrey: Here.

313
00:13:26,889 --> 00:13:27,389
There, look.

314
00:13:27,473 --> 00:13:28,098
Okay, okay.

315
00:13:28,766 --> 00:13:29,767
Group picture, group picture.

316
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:32,645
Ahh! Team Padua!

317
00:13:32,728 --> 00:13:34,104
Yeah!

318
00:13:34,188 --> 00:13:38,317
- Others: Yay!
- [exclaims & whoops]

319
00:13:38,400 --> 00:13:40,486
Jackpot!

320
00:13:40,569 --> 00:13:41,070
Yay!

321
00:13:41,779 --> 00:13:42,988
Jesabel: Okay, just go
straight there.

322
00:13:45,699 --> 00:13:47,785
This, this, this door right here.

323
00:13:47,868 --> 00:13:49,411
Open it, then go in.

324
00:13:49,495 --> 00:13:50,871
[door lock clicks]

325
00:13:53,749 --> 00:13:54,416
[light music playing]

326
00:13:54,500 --> 00:13:55,417
Beatriz…

327
00:13:57,086 --> 00:13:58,420
nice to see you again.

328
00:13:58,504 --> 00:13:59,630
[sighs]

329
00:13:59,713 --> 00:14:00,464
Same.

330
00:14:00,548 --> 00:14:02,007
I thought we'd never see each
other again.

331
00:14:04,343 --> 00:14:07,263
Where are Sir Atoy
and Emerson?

332
00:14:07,346 --> 00:14:10,683
Oh, Sir Atoy just dropped
that off earlier,

333
00:14:10,766 --> 00:14:12,726
because he was in a bit
of a hurry,

334
00:14:12,810 --> 00:14:15,521
since they were late for
the family activity.

335
00:14:16,564 --> 00:14:19,191
So, this is where
I'll be staying?

336
00:14:20,192 --> 00:14:23,696
Oh, why? Do you have a problem
with this place?

337
00:14:23,779 --> 00:14:24,697
I'm sorry, okay,

338
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:26,115
this isn't a five-star hotel.

339
00:14:27,116 --> 00:14:28,284
No, that's not
what I meant.

340
00:14:28,367 --> 00:14:30,035
I'm okay to be here.

341
00:14:30,119 --> 00:14:31,787
I'm just happy I'm alive.

342
00:14:32,580 --> 00:14:34,123
Ah, you're happy.

343
00:14:34,206 --> 00:14:34,915
[sneaky music playing]

344
00:14:34,999 --> 00:14:37,543
So, this girl speaks English, but…

345
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:39,837
didn't get a blow-dry,
looking haggard, huh.

346
00:14:40,671 --> 00:14:45,217
Ah, let me just
remind you, okay.

347
00:14:46,510 --> 00:14:48,304
That in this house…

348
00:14:49,388 --> 00:14:50,723
it's KKK.

349
00:14:50,806 --> 00:14:53,809
As in, everyone for themselves.

350
00:14:54,351 --> 00:14:55,769
Remember that, okay,

351
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:58,522
and I'm not a maid here…

352
00:14:59,398 --> 00:15:01,150
for you to order around, okay.

353
00:15:01,734 --> 00:15:03,402
Oh, look at my outfit.

354
00:15:03,903 --> 00:15:07,072
I'm a training tracker, tracker
in training, I mean.

355
00:15:07,656 --> 00:15:10,326
Okay, Jezebel.
Thanks for that.

356
00:15:10,409 --> 00:15:12,411
Oh. You're wrong again, bae.

357
00:15:12,494 --> 00:15:15,539
My name is Jesabel, not Jezebel.

358
00:15:16,582 --> 00:15:18,417
Okay, Donnabelle?

359
00:15:18,918 --> 00:15:23,088
Sorry, Jesabel and my name
is Belladonna,

360
00:15:23,172 --> 00:15:24,715
and if that's too long
for you,

361
00:15:24,798 --> 00:15:26,592
you can just call
me Beatriz.

362
00:15:26,675 --> 00:15:27,509
Oh, well--

363
00:15:27,593 --> 00:15:28,761
Mmm. Don't give her
attitude.

364
00:15:29,720 --> 00:15:30,804
Just relax.

365
00:15:31,472 --> 00:15:32,681
I'll take her on.

366
00:15:32,765 --> 00:15:34,391
No, Jezebel.

367
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:35,476
You too.

368
00:15:35,559 --> 00:15:37,728
Where could Emerson be?

369
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:39,438
It's still closed.

370
00:15:40,814 --> 00:15:43,067
The kids' family
day is over.

371
00:15:44,068 --> 00:15:45,194
Do you miss him?

372
00:15:45,778 --> 00:15:46,403
Aren't you mad at him anymore?

373
00:15:46,487 --> 00:15:48,822
Hey, hey. I didn't say anything like
that, you know.

374
00:15:48,906 --> 00:15:50,240
I'm just wondering,

375
00:15:50,324 --> 00:15:51,116
and I don't miss him.

376
00:15:55,663 --> 00:15:56,914
My Loves!

377
00:15:56,997 --> 00:15:57,498
[sighs]

378
00:15:58,040 --> 00:16:00,125
Brother Kurt, Brother Kurt.

379
00:16:00,876 --> 00:16:01,585
My Loves, My Loves!

380
00:16:01,669 --> 00:16:02,503
Why do you look like that?

381
00:16:02,586 --> 00:16:03,212
What happened to you?

382
00:16:03,295 --> 00:16:05,255
It's okay, it's okay.

383
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:06,298
I'm okay, My Loves.

384
00:16:06,382 --> 00:16:07,466
I know that…

385
00:16:07,549 --> 00:16:09,009
you're concerned about me,
so I'm okay.

386
00:16:09,093 --> 00:16:10,970
Wow, why are you so dirty?

387
00:16:12,096 --> 00:16:13,847
What, no-- it's-- it's nothing,
it's nothing.

388
00:16:13,931 --> 00:16:16,475
It's just that, we just
had a small…

389
00:16:16,558 --> 00:16:19,103
Atoy's mission.

390
00:16:19,186 --> 00:16:20,562
Emerson: But she's safe with
Jesabel now.

391
00:16:20,646 --> 00:16:21,647
- Mission?
- Denden: Jesabel?

392
00:16:21,730 --> 00:16:25,734
- Emerson: Yes. Yes. Oh, no!
- You were with Jesabel again?

393
00:16:26,443 --> 00:16:27,695
Oh, yes. Ah--

394
00:16:27,778 --> 00:16:28,904
[sneaky music playing]

395
00:16:28,988 --> 00:16:30,531
Oh, ah-- what, ah…

396
00:16:30,614 --> 00:16:31,615
Sorry, sorry, sorry.

397
00:16:31,699 --> 00:16:32,449
Sorry, My Loves.

398
00:16:32,533 --> 00:16:35,369
No. What-- what I mean is, um…

399
00:16:35,452 --> 00:16:37,955
What, ah, don't-- don't be
mad anymore, please.

400
00:16:38,038 --> 00:16:38,914
Here, here, look.

401
00:16:38,998 --> 00:16:41,417
I even brought you, um, flo--

402
00:16:42,501 --> 00:16:44,420
- This is… Bopis for our meal…
- Where's the--

403
00:16:44,503 --> 00:16:46,213
Why did you bring something
for tinola?

404
00:16:46,296 --> 00:16:47,381
[chuckles]

405
00:16:47,464 --> 00:16:48,132
Oh, no.

406
00:16:48,215 --> 00:16:49,341
These aren’t shoots, um--

407
00:16:49,425 --> 00:16:50,342
The-- there are flowers--

408
00:16:50,426 --> 00:16:52,094
They've been through
a lot, you see.

409
00:16:52,678 --> 00:16:53,429
- Let's just throw them away.
- Thank you, thank you-

410
00:16:53,512 --> 00:16:55,305
It's okay.
Thank you, My Loves!

411
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:56,724
What matters is
you're safe.

412
00:16:56,807 --> 00:16:58,892
- Okay, okay. I'm safe. Okay.
-

413
00:16:58,976 --> 00:16:59,852
[both chuckle]

414
00:16:59,935 --> 00:17:01,020
Oh, sweet.

415
00:17:01,562 --> 00:17:02,813
So, so sweet.

416
00:17:02,896 --> 00:17:03,939
[pleasant music playing]

417
00:17:04,023 --> 00:17:04,815
Thank you, thank you.

418
00:17:04,898 --> 00:17:06,525
You're the flowers,
look. Hmm.

419
00:17:06,608 --> 00:17:07,317
[giggles]

420
00:17:07,401 --> 00:17:08,027
My Loves, really.

421
00:17:08,110 --> 00:17:08,986
[music fades]

422
00:17:09,069 --> 00:17:09,695
Wait a moment, okay.

423
00:17:09,778 --> 00:17:11,321
This cake has been…

424
00:17:11,405 --> 00:17:12,781
staring at me for
a while now.

425
00:17:12,865 --> 00:17:13,699
Let's taste it, let's
taste it.

426
00:17:14,283 --> 00:17:15,451
There! Okay, okay!

427
00:17:15,534 --> 00:17:17,077
That's the best, really!

428
00:17:17,161 --> 00:17:17,703
[chuckles]

429
00:17:17,786 --> 00:17:19,163
Thank you, ah!

430
00:17:19,246 --> 00:17:20,998
I'll just use this fork.

431
00:17:23,667 --> 00:17:25,252
Mmm.

432
00:17:25,335 --> 00:17:28,630
Plate, plate. You, Janine?
Where's your plate?

433
00:17:28,714 --> 00:17:29,381
- Ah, here.
- Audrey: Plate, plate.

434
00:17:29,465 --> 00:17:30,382
Ibyang: Give me a plate.

435
00:17:33,052 --> 00:17:36,847
[lively chatter, laughing]

436
00:17:37,848 --> 00:17:38,932
Come, come, come.

437
00:17:39,016 --> 00:17:39,558
Audrey: Mmm, there.

438
00:17:39,641 --> 00:17:41,018
Oscar: Okay.
That’s for you.

439
00:17:41,101 --> 00:17:41,769
Ibyang: So delicious. Oh.

440
00:17:41,852 --> 00:17:43,479
This, this whole piece
is mine.

441
00:17:43,562 --> 00:17:46,106
Oh no. Wow--

442
00:17:46,190 --> 00:17:48,025
[lively chatter]

443
00:17:48,108 --> 00:17:49,359
This is mine, in case
it runs out--

444
00:17:49,443 --> 00:17:51,445
Whoa!

445
00:17:51,528 --> 00:17:52,821
[exclaims]

446
00:17:53,322 --> 00:17:55,199
Mmm. Hey, it's delicious, ah.

447
00:17:55,282 --> 00:17:57,076
You too, Team Padua!

448
00:17:57,951 --> 00:17:59,828
Team Padua's signature!

449
00:18:00,537 --> 00:18:01,163
[Oscar whoops]

450
00:18:01,246 --> 00:18:03,624
[music continues]

451
00:18:08,128 --> 00:18:10,547
I don’t get any, because the
cake is mine.

452
00:18:10,631 --> 00:18:12,966
Ah, wow! Wow!

453
00:18:13,050 --> 00:18:14,218
Yes. Do you want some? Okay.

454
00:18:14,301 --> 00:18:15,094
It's Big Sis Ame.

455
00:18:15,177 --> 00:18:16,136
Put the cake here.

456
00:18:16,512 --> 00:18:18,555
Ame: I'm not part of it.
No, no, no.

457
00:18:18,639 --> 00:18:19,723
Tatoy?

458
00:18:19,807 --> 00:18:22,434
[overlapping chatter]

459
00:18:22,518 --> 00:18:23,685
Tatoy!

460
00:18:23,769 --> 00:18:24,728
Hmm!

461
00:18:25,270 --> 00:18:26,271
[giggles]

462
00:18:27,397 --> 00:18:29,316
Oh. Where did you
come from?

463
00:18:29,900 --> 00:18:30,776
Mmm. Sorry.

464
00:18:30,859 --> 00:18:31,568
Hello, hello.

465
00:18:31,652 --> 00:18:33,195
Mmm. Mmm…

466
00:18:33,278 --> 00:18:34,446
[smooches]

467
00:18:34,530 --> 00:18:36,281
Oh. Sorry, sorry.

468
00:18:41,328 --> 00:18:42,538
Good thing you're home
already.

469
00:18:44,206 --> 00:18:45,249
Sorry, okay.

470
00:18:45,332 --> 00:18:47,584
I wasn't able to make it to
Ibyang and Janine's event.

471
00:18:48,585 --> 00:18:49,586
Why, though?

472
00:18:50,838 --> 00:18:53,257
There was a, there was
a mishap with the--

473
00:18:55,050 --> 00:18:57,177
Sorry. I-- I made a mistake.

474
00:18:58,220 --> 00:18:59,930
Atoy: So, sorry, okay.
Sorry to all of you.

475
00:19:01,723 --> 00:19:02,891
Love, I'm sorry.

476
00:19:03,684 --> 00:19:05,894
Sorry, sorry, okay.
Sorry, okay.

477
00:19:05,978 --> 00:19:06,895
I wasn't able to make it.

478
00:19:07,896 --> 00:19:11,358
Tatoy, one sorry is enough.

479
00:19:12,442 --> 00:19:15,904
Oh, just join us in
the celebration.

480
00:19:18,574 --> 00:19:19,283
Okay.

481
00:19:19,783 --> 00:19:21,535
Janine: Daddy, look.

482
00:19:23,287 --> 00:19:24,705
We're the champions!

483
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:25,706
Wow!

484
00:19:25,789 --> 00:19:26,498
Champion.

485
00:19:26,582 --> 00:19:28,375
That's so great!

486
00:19:28,458 --> 00:19:30,294
Wow! Congratulations!

487
00:19:30,377 --> 00:19:32,129
[music continues]

488
00:19:33,755 --> 00:19:38,302
It's a pity though, because…
you weren't here.

489
00:19:39,636 --> 00:19:42,055
But good thing Uncle Oka
was there.

490
00:19:42,139 --> 00:19:43,015
Yeah.

491
00:19:43,098 --> 00:19:45,350
Oh, he subbed for you.

492
00:19:45,434 --> 00:19:46,643
He was so great.

493
00:19:47,561 --> 00:19:50,898
Both: Uncle Oka! Uncle Oka!

494
00:19:50,981 --> 00:19:51,481
What are you saying?

495
00:19:51,565 --> 00:19:52,941
It was because of you two, geez.

496
00:19:53,025 --> 00:19:54,109
- Both: Uncle Oka!
- It was you, you--

497
00:19:54,985 --> 00:19:58,780
Buddy, we really just
enjoyed the games,

498
00:19:58,864 --> 00:20:00,824
and these kids are just flattering
me, you know. Mmm.

499
00:20:00,908 --> 00:20:01,909
Atoy: Great.

500
00:20:02,826 --> 00:20:03,952
Very good.

501
00:20:04,953 --> 00:20:07,581
[pensive music playing]

502
00:20:07,664 --> 00:20:10,292
Yes, indeed. Ah, Tatoy,
what's that?

503
00:20:10,375 --> 00:20:12,169
Oh, this is your
mommy's favorite.

504
00:20:13,003 --> 00:20:14,796
[music continues]

505
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:15,464
Too late.

506
00:20:16,256 --> 00:20:17,633
Oka already bought one.

507
00:20:17,716 --> 00:20:19,760
Ah, bu-- but, Love,
this is the OG,

508
00:20:19,843 --> 00:20:21,845
your favorite, the one
from-- Batangas.

509
00:20:21,929 --> 00:20:23,847
The one we always went
to back then.

510
00:20:23,931 --> 00:20:24,514
Remember?

511
00:20:25,098 --> 00:20:26,141
I'm full.

512
00:20:27,100 --> 00:20:27,643
Janine: Oh.

513
00:20:28,143 --> 00:20:30,896
[music continues]

514
00:20:38,695 --> 00:20:42,157
[music fades]

515
00:20:44,868 --> 00:20:46,203
[utensils clatter]

516
00:20:49,206 --> 00:20:51,500
Is there still room in the
fridge for this?

517
00:20:53,252 --> 00:20:54,002
Check.

518
00:20:59,174 --> 00:21:00,717
Are you still sulking
because of me?

519
00:21:01,635 --> 00:21:02,427
Sulking?

520
00:21:03,053 --> 00:21:05,222
Sulking is only for
kids, Atoy.

521
00:21:05,973 --> 00:21:08,850
How many times did I tell you not
to miss family day.

522
00:21:08,934 --> 00:21:10,394
But what happened, huh?

523
00:21:10,477 --> 00:21:11,603
You promised!

524
00:21:12,354 --> 00:21:13,272
But you weren't there!

525
00:21:13,939 --> 00:21:15,607
Good thing Oka was there.

526
00:21:16,149 --> 00:21:18,735
[music continues]

527
00:21:18,819 --> 00:21:19,945
Yes, indeed.

528
00:21:21,029 --> 00:21:22,864
Good thing Oka was
there, right?

529
00:21:22,948 --> 00:21:24,449
[music continues]

530
00:21:24,533 --> 00:21:26,201
Atoy: It looks like you all
enjoyed yourselves.

531
00:21:27,703 --> 00:21:29,329
And it doesn't look like
you missed me.

532
00:21:29,413 --> 00:21:30,539
Especially you.

533
00:21:30,622 --> 00:21:33,292
You didn't even kiss me earlier
when I arrived.

534
00:21:33,375 --> 00:21:36,628
Oh, you're the one who has the
nerve to feel hurt?

535
00:21:37,212 --> 00:21:37,963
Anthony Padua,

536
00:21:38,046 --> 00:21:39,506
don't turn the situation around

537
00:21:39,589 --> 00:21:41,133
because you're the one
who didn't come!

538
00:21:41,758 --> 00:21:43,927
At least Oka is reliable!

539
00:21:44,511 --> 00:21:46,013
Even if he's not the father
and husband

540
00:21:46,096 --> 00:21:47,180
in this house.

541
00:21:48,015 --> 00:21:49,683
[music continues]

542
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:51,435
Audrey.

543
00:21:52,311 --> 00:21:54,438
[music continues]

544
00:21:55,355 --> 00:21:56,106
Sorry.

545
00:21:56,732 --> 00:21:58,775
[music continues]

546
00:22:00,110 --> 00:22:01,486
I'll just go outside.

547
00:22:02,529 --> 00:22:03,989
I thought the cake was going
in the fridge?

548
00:22:05,282 --> 00:22:07,409
I'll just give this cake to someone
who will appreciate it.

549
00:22:07,492 --> 00:22:10,162
[melodramatic music playing]

550
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:25,010
Hmm. This coconut cake Atoy
brought is so delicious.

551
00:22:25,093 --> 00:22:26,261
The best!

552
00:22:26,344 --> 00:22:27,679
Hmm, oh my.

553
00:22:27,763 --> 00:22:31,808
If you only knew what Atoy
went through.

554
00:22:31,892 --> 00:22:35,687
Actually, what we went through just
to bring home this cake.

555
00:22:36,646 --> 00:22:38,690
I walked so far to get this.

556
00:22:39,399 --> 00:22:41,026
Hmm, but…

557
00:22:42,319 --> 00:22:43,570
the sad part is…

558
00:22:44,821 --> 00:22:46,198
when he got home…

559
00:22:46,782 --> 00:22:50,494
He saw Audrey and the rest were
eating a cake already…

560
00:22:51,286 --> 00:22:55,082
because Oka was
showing off.

561
00:22:55,165 --> 00:22:57,876
Wow! Meaning, they already
have two cakes?

562
00:23:00,003 --> 00:23:01,671
Oka is so kind!

563
00:23:01,755 --> 00:23:02,297
Correct!

564
00:23:02,380 --> 00:23:03,298
- Mmm-mmm.
- My Loves, c’mon.

565
00:23:03,381 --> 00:23:05,759
What I mean is,

566
00:23:05,842 --> 00:23:09,679
Oka is such a showoff, acting
like the hero!

567
00:23:10,764 --> 00:23:11,556
Siony: Hmm.

568
00:23:11,640 --> 00:23:12,808
Then…

569
00:23:13,475 --> 00:23:15,936
when Atoy arrived, of
course he saw it.

570
00:23:16,019 --> 00:23:16,520
Siony: Mmm?

571
00:23:17,187 --> 00:23:18,980
He bought the cake for
his wife and kids,

572
00:23:19,064 --> 00:23:20,565
why would Oka meddle, right?

573
00:23:20,649 --> 00:23:22,067
Is he even their family?

574
00:23:22,150 --> 00:23:23,693
Naturally, the man was hurt

575
00:23:23,777 --> 00:23:25,362
when he saw that…

576
00:23:26,029 --> 00:23:27,280
there was already
a cake at home.

577
00:23:27,364 --> 00:23:30,659
It feels like his effort
was disregarded.

578
00:23:30,742 --> 00:23:31,243
Siony: Is that so?

579
00:23:31,326 --> 00:23:32,035
Mmm-hmm.

580
00:23:32,911 --> 00:23:36,164
And then, he wasn't able to go to

581
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:37,749
the family day of the…

582
00:23:37,833 --> 00:23:39,167
the kids.

583
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:40,293
Siony: Mmm?

584
00:23:40,377 --> 00:23:41,128
There, see.

585
00:23:41,211 --> 00:23:43,380
Now they're fighting,
him and Au-- Audrey

586
00:23:43,922 --> 00:23:45,757
Both: Hmm.

587
00:23:45,841 --> 00:23:47,801
I'm sure the two of them
will fix that.

588
00:23:48,468 --> 00:23:49,803
So, for us, My Loves,

589
00:23:49,886 --> 00:23:51,972
let's promise
each other that…

590
00:23:52,055 --> 00:23:54,307
when we have a problem, we'll fix
it right away, okay.

591
00:23:54,391 --> 00:23:58,395
By being honest and open with
each other, right?

592
00:23:58,478 --> 00:23:59,729
I'll try my best.

593
00:24:00,355 --> 00:24:02,732
Of course, I promise.
Promise, of course.

594
00:24:02,816 --> 00:24:04,109
So, what did you and Atoy
do, by the way?

595
00:24:04,192 --> 00:24:05,360
Why were you gone
for so long?

596
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:07,112
Denden: Huh?

597
00:24:08,113 --> 00:24:12,033
Honestly, this cake
is so delicious.

598
00:24:12,117 --> 00:24:13,118
This is the best.

599
00:24:13,201 --> 00:24:15,412
Yes, really. I walked so
far to get this.

600
00:24:16,538 --> 00:24:17,414
This is really delicious.

601
00:24:17,497 --> 00:24:19,332
Siony: So delicious,
the best!

602
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:23,712
Emerson: Samir's man is here.

603
00:24:23,795 --> 00:24:25,088
Atoy: I know, they're
here too.

604
00:24:25,172 --> 00:24:25,881
Emerson: Huh?!

605
00:24:25,964 --> 00:24:27,257
What, they have an
advance party?

606
00:24:28,049 --> 00:24:30,177
Why do they know where
Belladonna is?

607
00:24:36,433 --> 00:24:37,893
[phone blipping]

608
00:24:42,230 --> 00:24:45,317
[music continues]

609
00:24:49,821 --> 00:24:53,575
[tense music playing]

610
00:24:53,658 --> 00:24:59,539
[phone blipping]

611
00:25:07,047 --> 00:25:08,840
I knew it.

612
00:25:10,008 --> 00:25:11,635
Son of a thread.

613
00:25:11,718 --> 00:25:14,221
[music swells]

614
00:25:14,304 --> 00:25:18,475
[electronic blipping]

615
00:25:18,558 --> 00:25:22,479
[intense music playing]

616
00:25:24,105 --> 00:25:26,608
Shugo: Atoy went inside
the laundry shop,

617
00:25:26,691 --> 00:25:29,903
but we didn't see when
he came out.

618
00:25:29,986 --> 00:25:32,822
Do you think he's the one who
burned the laundry shop?

619
00:25:32,906 --> 00:25:35,742
We'll corner you soon, Atoy.

620
00:25:35,825 --> 00:25:37,202
You have no way out.

621
00:25:37,285 --> 00:25:39,579
We'd like to invite you to
the station again.

622
00:25:39,663 --> 00:25:41,373
I am out of patience.

623
00:25:41,456 --> 00:25:43,416
So, for your own sake,

624
00:25:44,084 --> 00:25:47,254
tell me everything about
the Belladonna.

625
00:25:47,337 --> 00:25:48,338
Samir: Make them talk!

626
00:25:48,421 --> 00:25:51,049
[electricity buzzing]

627
00:25:51,925 --> 00:25:54,386
Audrey: Love…

628
00:25:54,469 --> 00:25:56,096
Siony: That's why I'm telling
you, Audrey,

629
00:25:56,179 --> 00:25:58,139
keep an eye on Atoy.

630
00:25:58,723 --> 00:25:59,307
Why?

631
00:26:00,016 --> 00:26:01,393
Because my cousin here,

632
00:26:01,476 --> 00:26:03,436
Siony: is always talking
to someone else

633
00:26:03,520 --> 00:26:04,896
and texting someone else.

634
00:26:04,980 --> 00:26:08,275
And he brings his phone even
to the bathroom,

635
00:26:08,358 --> 00:26:11,069
and also, they say they're
no longer…

636
00:26:11,820 --> 00:26:13,363
doing the loving-loving.

637
00:26:14,030 --> 00:26:16,032
One of my last tasks
for Obsidian

638
00:26:16,116 --> 00:26:18,368
was to create specialized
long-ranged guns.

639
00:26:18,451 --> 00:26:19,828
Part of the Big Bang
Plot apparently.

640
00:26:19,911 --> 00:26:21,162
What could that
Big Bang be?

641
00:26:21,246 --> 00:26:23,790
But before Samir came
here to Manila,

642
00:26:23,873 --> 00:26:25,792
I met with a certain
Sir Ronan.

643
00:26:25,875 --> 00:26:27,836
Belladonna: They call him
The Manager.

644
00:26:27,919 --> 00:26:30,171
Are you Ronan Santos?

645
00:26:31,047 --> 00:26:31,589
Mate.

646
00:26:32,173 --> 00:26:34,759
So, what's the business loan for
Mr. Teddy Santos?

647
00:26:34,843 --> 00:26:38,555
["Mamang Sastre" playing]
